From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kan Zhu <kanzhu@cs.washington.edu>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 04:09:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/18] moe: capture the MTP drafter's routes under model
 runner V2

A token corpus for an MTP deployment needs the drafter layer's routes: the
simulator prices the MTP MoE from its own slice. Upstream sizes the capture
buffer by the target's layers and binds only the target, so those routes
never reach the client.

- Size the buffer for an MTP drafter's layers (they start at the target's
  layer count) and only for method "mtp"; any other drafter would leave a
  slot nothing writes.
- Bind the single-module MTP drafter. Refuse a multi-module drafter, whose
  later layers see one row per request instead of token rows.
- Keep the draft prefill's routes. Later draft passes run one row per
  request and would overwrite the first num_reqs token rows from inside the
  CUDA graph, so the speculator holds the drafter's slots after prefill and
  restores them after decoding.
- The step's routes are snapshotted right after the target forward, when the
  drafter's slots still hold the previous step. With a bound drafter the
  runner fills those slots after propose and only then starts the D2H copy.
- The alignment routing dump runs before the drafter too, so it skips the
  drafter's slots.
- Model runner V1 does not bind the drafter, so it refuses MTP capture
  rather than returning zero routes.

Rebased onto upstream 04730e8, where routed-experts capture moved into
the V2-only AuxOutput connector: the drafter is bound when the connector
is created, the draft slots are refreshed in the connector's pending
snapshot, and AsyncOutput.copy_aux_output starts the deferred D2H copy.
V1 can no longer return routes upstream, so its MTP refusal is dropped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
